As a baseline, we devised a simple linear model. It represents each read-out gene with a K-dimensional vector and each perturbation with an L-dimensional vector. These vectors are collected in the matrices G, with one row per read-out gene, and P, with one row per perturbation. G and P are either obtained as dimension-reducing embeddings of the training data (Methods) or provided by an external source (see below). Then, given a data matrix Ytrain of gene expression values, with one row per read-out gene and one column per perturbation (that is, per condition pseudobulk of the single-cell data), the K × L matrix W is found as1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
