The additive model is a special case of the linear model (equation (1)) where the gene embedding is simply the single perturbation data, without any further transformation or dimension reduction (G = Ysingle); the perturbation embedding P is a binary coding, where each column vector has 1s in the rows of the perturbed genes and is 0 otherwise; and W is an identity matrix and \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
