				\begin{document}$${{\rm{TPR}}}_{l}=\frac{\mathop{\sum }\nolimits_{i = 1}^{l}{\boldsymbol{1}}(\mathrm{abs}\,{({\bf{Y}}-{\hat{{\bf{Y}}}}^{{\rm{add}}})}_{{{\boldsymbol{j}}}_{i}}\ge u)}{\mathop{\sum }\nolimits_{i = 1}^{N}{\boldsymbol{1}}(\mathrm{abs}\,{({\bf{Y}}-{\hat{{\bf{Y}}}}^{{\rm{add}}})}_{i}\ge u)},$$\end{document}TPRl=∑i=1l1(abs(Y−Y^add)ji≥u)∑i=1N1(abs(Y−Y^add)i≥u),where Y is the matrix of observed value and N is the product of the number of genes and perturbations. The indicator function 1( ⋅ ) counts how often the observed values Y deviate enough from the additive expectation so that the observations are considered an interaction. The order statistic j ensures that we consider the gene–perturbation pairs first, where the model prediction deviates most from the additive expectation.

